      "content": "It's incredibly frustrating when you feel like the standard advice isn't touching the deep, systemic weight of your problems. When everything feels broken, the pressure to \"fix\" it all at once can be crushing. Maybe instead of trying to fix the whole life, could you focus on just one tiny thing to relieve some immediate pressure? Even a small, manageable change can sometimes break the inertia of the loop.",
      "source": "target",
